<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">South America</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">South America is a continent in the Western Hemisphere, colonised mainly by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and Portugal from the sixteenth century. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, the largest country, became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a> after independence in 1822. The Brazilian Empire profile discusses its wars and influence in the continent, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paraguayan-war">Paraguayan War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/south-america.jpg" alt="South America" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: derivative work: Luan by Luan · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:South_America_(orthographic_projection).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
